; Sprites: crowned creature, dome, bars, spotted ball
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $B700+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. Frames 0-1 look like a creature with a crown and raised prongs
; (entities $30-$32 in The Kitchen, room $17, and West of Kitchen, room $18). Frames 2-3 look like a striped dome
; (entities $1F, $33). Frame 4 is a narrow bar pattern and frames 5-7 a spotted ball turning (entity $5C, frames 4-7).
; Used by entity definitions $1F $30 $31 $32 $33 $5C in rooms $16 $17 $18 $2E $34 $37 $39.
@label=SpritesCrownDomeBall
